PR 2's incumbent/v2/worker.json (same bytes as tuner/worker.json) fails `researchworld worker check`: "holds what a worker does not: worker (a published worker is what a position sets for itself under worker.roles.POSITION, not a world's run settings)". Unwrapping the `worker` key and dropping backend, max_attempts, max_executions, max_model_seconds, overspend, roles, image, environment_image, environment_network gives a file that passes ('publishable': true). Contents that passed:

```json
{
 "acpx": {},
 "agent": "claude-code",
 "assets": [],
 "build_timeout_sec": 600.0,
 "claude_code": {
  "env": {
   "CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL": "low"
  }
 },
 "limits": {
  "cpus": 2.0,
  "gpus": 0,
  "memory_mb": 4096,
  "processes": 256,
  "temporary_mb": 512
 },
 "max_context_fraction": 0.6,
 "max_turn_model_sec": null,
 "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
 "no_progress_sec": 1800.0,
 "opencode": {
  "share": "disabled",
  "update": "disable"
 },
 "provider": {
  "auth": "claude-oauth",
  "base_url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1",
  "id": "anthropic-claude-code",
  "protocol": "anthropic"
 },
 "provider_backpressure": {
  "failure_threshold": 2,
  "hold_sec": 240,
  "initial_cooldown_sec": 30,
  "max_cooldown_sec": 900,
  "request_timeout_sec": 120,
  "retry_attempts": 3
 },
 "provider_fallbacks": [],
 "provider_profile": null,
 "provider_profiles": {}
}
```
Please make worker.json in tuner's repo exactly this (flat worker settings, and per the check's message possibly under worker.roles.<position> if the publish format needs it, but run the check yourself) and update PR 2. The put-back round ran (world rw_935fcb416784, evaluation/round2.md) and the incumbent is kept.

HUTIAN_REVIEW_DECISION: {"conclusion":"PR 2 worker.json fails worker check; deliver a publishable worker.json.","disposition":"revise","evidence":["researchworld worker check on PR 2 file","evaluation/round2.md"]}
